1. Title: Default of Credit Card Clients (25 January 2016)

2. Sources:
-- I-Cheng Yeh (creator)
   UCI Machine Learning Repository
   Irvine, California
   USA
-- Date: January 25, 2016
-- URL: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/350/default+of+credit+card+clients

3. Relevant Information:
   The dataset contains variables and information of 30,000 clients in Taiwan. There are variables about demographics, credit limit, payment hisotry, and bill statement amounts. This dataset will be used to predict if clients will default on their credit card using various models.

4. Number of Instances: 30,000 (as of 25 January 2016)

5. Number of Attributes: 23

6. Attribute Information: 
   #   Attribute
   ------------------------
   X1. ID - Identification Number
   X2. SEX - 1 for Male, 2 for Female
   X3. EDUCATION - 1 = graduate school; 2 = university; 3 = high school; 4 = others
   X4: MARRIAGE - 1 = married; 2 = single; 3 = others
   X5: AGE - year
   X6: PAY_0 - repayment status in September, 2005
   X7: PAY_2 - repyament status in August, 2005
   X8:
- X11: History of past payment. We tracked the past monthly payment records (from April to September, 2005) as follows: X6 = the repayment status in September, 2005; X7 = the repayment status in August, 2005; . . .;X11 = the repayment status in April, 2005. The measurement scale for the repayment status is: -1 = pay duly; 1 = payment delay for one month; 2 = payment delay for two months; . . .; 8 = payment delay for eight months; 9 = payment delay for nine months and above.


